{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sorted sets share one API: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"type":"text","text":"’s set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operations, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowerBound(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"upperBound(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the elements as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank. Changing which one a program uses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a change of type name:"}]},{"code":["let avl: AVLTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let redBlack: RedBlackTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let bTree: BTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let skipList: SkipList = [40, 10, 30, 20]","","Array(avl)              \/\/ [10, 20, 30, 40], and the same for the others","avl.lowerBound(25)      \/\/ 2, the index of 30","bTree.lowerBound(25)    \/\/ 2"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one takes O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") per lookup, insertion and removal (expected for the treap and skip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list, amortized for the splay tree). They differ in the constant, in what else they offer, and in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which workloads they suit."}]},{"anchor":"Lookups-and-scans-over-a-large-set-BTree","level":3,"text":"Lookups and scans over a large set: BTree","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A B-tree node ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") holds tens of elements side by side, so a lookup reads a few nodes and few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cache lines, and iteration walks contiguous arrays. For a large set that is read far more often"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than it is changed, and for range scans, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default. Copying a B-tree shares its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes, and a mutated copy copies only the nodes on the path it changes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its sorted dictionary."}]},{"anchor":"Balanced-binary-trees-AVLTree-and-RedBlackTree","level":3,"text":"Balanced binary trees: AVLTree and RedBlackTree","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"AVLTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the heights of every vertex’s subtrees within one of each other, so it is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shallowest of the binary trees and the quickest of them to search. A "},{"code":"RedBlackTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" allows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taller tree and in return rotates at most two or three times per insertion or removal; prefer it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when changes outnumber lookups. Both convert to a Grafluent "},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that shows the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape. "},{"code":"AVLDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary in an AVL tree."}]},{"anchor":"Splitting-and-joining-Treap","level":3,"text":"Splitting and joining: Treap","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"Treap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a random priority on each vertex, which makes its shape a random binary search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree’s whatever order the elements arrive in, and gives it "},{"code":"split(at:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"join(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["let numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OverlappingKeys"},{"type":"text","text":" when the sets interleave. Pass a seeded generator to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap(_:using:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to make every shape reproducible. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"type":"text","text":" splits too."}]},{"anchor":"A-working-set-of-hot-elements-SplayTree","level":3,"text":"A working set of hot elements: SplayTree","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps no balance information. "},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and each mutation rotate the element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they reach to the root, so a run of lookups that keeps returning to a few elements finds them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"near the top:"}]},{"code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its other reads, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" among them, leave the tree as it is, so they keep value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantics; use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"access(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" where the splay is wanted."}]},{"anchor":"A-sorted-queue-with-a-simple-structure-SkipList","level":3,"text":"A sorted queue with a simple structure: SkipList","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A skip list (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") stacks sorted linked levels, each holding about half the elements of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the one below. Its insertions touch only the levels an element reaches, and its levels are a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent graph through ","type":"text"},{"code":"layersView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Keeping-every-version-PersistentTreeSet","level":3,"text":"Keeping every version: PersistentTreeSet","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When old versions must stay readable, as in undo histories, snapshots handed to other tasks or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking searches, a persistent set ("},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") shares all but the vertices an edit touched:"}]},{"code":["let empty = PersistentTreeSet<Int>()","let one = empty.inserting(5)","let two = one.inserting(3)","let three = two.removing(5)","Array(one)                    \/\/ [5]","Array(two)                    \/\/ [3, 5]","Array(three)                  \/\/ [3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each version costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") new vertices rather than a copy of the whole tree."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary."}]},{"anchor":"Summary","level":3,"text":"Summary","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Workload"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Large sets, mostly lookups, range scans"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly lookups, a binary shape to inspect"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"AVLTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AVLDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly insertions and removals"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"RedBlackTree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splitting and joining sets"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Treap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Repeated access to a few elements"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every version kept","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PersistentTreeSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistentTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A simple sorted queue","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SkipList","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Pick a sorted set or sorted dictionary by the workload it will see.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/choosingasearchtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Choosing a search tree","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/skiplists":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","title":"SkipLists","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkipLists"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/DecisionDiagrams":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/decisiondiagrams","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represent Boolean functions and families of sets as shared, canonical graphs."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","title":"Decision diagrams","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/persistenttrees":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","title":"PersistentTrees","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTrees"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph","abstract":[{"text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over it.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","title":"GrafluentCollections","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/RangeAndSpatialTrees":{"title":"Range and spatial trees","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Answer queries over ranges of a sequence, over intervals, and over points in space."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/rangeandspatialtrees","kind":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","title":"Tries and suffix structures","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/btrees":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","title":"BTrees","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTrees"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"}}}